  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Shengmating and the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein, mediated through the PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2. This protein is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, cocaine, and [4-Hydroxy-2-(3-methylbut-2-enyl)phenyl] 2,4-dihydroxy-6-methylbenzoate. These compounds are all predicted to interact with CDC2L2, which in turn is predicted to target the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent pattern of interaction, with varying levels of confidence, but all pointing to a shared pathway involving CDC2L2 as a critical mediator. The evidence suggests that Shengmating may influence the expression or activity of CDC2L2, which then affects the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein, potentially through kinase-mediated signaling. The mechanisms are consistent across the paths, but the strength of the evidence varies, with some paths showing higher confidence in the interaction.",
